      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The main issue you'd run into with trying to run PC content on a different platform is going to be shaders and texture formats. \n\nLike if I posted an avatar that is PC only, but using the VRChat mobile shaders, and a reasonable texture size (2k) and under 20k polygons, trying to force that avatar to work on a Quest would be sufficiently difficult to overload it. \n\nOr to look at the reverse, there is a reason you can't just upload an avatar as Quest, and see it on PC, that shader and texture stuff would really drag down the PC. Also the meshes. Pretend I didn't forget about the meshes until the end of my comment ;)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
